{"id":"043926d6-5259-43aa-8e53-5a85f68620fe","object":"chat.completion","created":1784991993,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    initial = case['initial_state']\\n    max_steps = case['max_steps']\\n    tool_obs = case['tool_observations']\\n    trans = case['transitions']\\n    state = initial\\n    step = 0\\n    trace = []\\n    while step < max_steps:\\n        if state not in trans:\\n            break\\n        obj = trans[state]\\n        if obj['kind'] == 'final':\\n            return {\\n                'final': obj['value'],\\n                'status': 'completed',\\n                'trace': trace\\n            }\\n        # action state\\n        action = obj['action']\\n        observation = tool_obs.get(action, 'invalid')\\n        trace.append({\\n            'step': step,\\n            'state': state,\\n            'action': action,\\n            'observation': observation\\n        })\\n        next_state = obj['next_by_observation'].get(observation, obj['default_next'])\\n        state = next_state\\n        step += 1\\n    return {\\n        'final': None,\\n        'status': 'max_steps',\\n        'trace': trace\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) for task AGENT-RA-02. The case payload contains:\n- initial_state: string\n- max_steps: integer\n- tool_observations: dict mapping tool name to observation string (presumably the observation produced when that tool is called)\n- transitions: dict mapping state name to state object. Each state object has:\n  - kind: \"action\" or \"final\"\n  - if action: action (string, tool name), next_by_observation (dict mapping observation to next state), default_next (string, fallback)\n  - if final: value (string, presumably the final answer)\n\nWe need to simulate a ReAct loop:\n- Start at initial_state.\n- Keep track of step count (starting at 0? The trace steps should be 0-inde